Travix AI — Database Migrations
================================

All schema changes are managed with Alembic. Every migration is a Python file
in ``migrations/versions/``. Run all commands from ``apps/api/``.


Quick Reference
---------------

Apply all pending migrations:
    alembic upgrade head

Generate a new migration from ORM model changes:
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe what changed"

Roll back one migration:
    alembic downgrade -1

Roll back to a specific revision:
    alembic downgrade <revision_id>

Show migration history:
    alembic history --verbose

Show current revision applied to the database:
    alembic current

Preview the SQL without applying it:
    alembic upgrade head --sql

Check that the DB schema matches the ORM models (CI gate):
    alembic check


Adding a New Model
------------------

1. Create the ORM model in ``app/modules/<module>/models.py``.
2. Import the model in ``migrations/env.py`` under the "Import all models" section.
3. Generate the migration:
       alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add <table_name> table"
4. Review the generated file in ``migrations/versions/``.
5. Work through the migration checklist in the file header.
6. Apply and verify locally:
       alembic upgrade head


Migration Checklist
-------------------

Every generated migration file contains a checklist. Before merging, verify:

  [ ] Auto-generated DDL is correct (review column types, constraints, defaults)
  [ ] GiST index added for every PostGIS geometry column
  [ ] updated_at trigger added for every new table
  [ ] soft-delete column (deleted_at) present for user-facing entities
  [ ] ON DELETE behaviour declared on all foreign keys (CASCADE / SET NULL / RESTRICT)
  [ ] downgrade() fully reverses upgrade() with no data loss (where possible)
  [ ] Tested upgrade AND downgrade locally before committing


Rules
-----

NEVER edit a migration file after it has been committed to the repository.
A migration that has been applied to staging or production is immutable.
If a migration contains an error, create a NEW migration that corrects it.

NEVER use ``Base.metadata.create_all()`` or ``drop_all()`` in application code.
These are reserved for test setup only (``tests/conftest.py``).

NEVER squash or rebase migrations. The version history must be linear and
complete for safe rollback in production.


Local Development Setup
-----------------------

1. Start the database:
       docker compose up postgres -d

2. Apply all migrations:
       alembic upgrade head

3. After changing a model, generate a migration:
       alembic revision --autogenerate -m "your description"


PostGIS Geometry Columns
------------------------

Alembic does not auto-detect PostGIS geometry columns correctly. When adding
a geometry column, write the migration manually using the postgis_ops module:

    from geoalchemy2 import Geometry

    op.add_column(
        "destinations",
        sa.Column("coordinates", Geometry("POINT", srid=4326), nullable=True),
    )

    # GiST index is REQUIRED for every geometry column (CLAUDE.md §10)
    op.create_index(
        "gix_destinations_coordinates",
        "destinations",
        ["coordinates"],
        postgresql_using="gist",
    )
